.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH orbit-import 1  "import " 
.SH NAME
orbit\-import \- Bring data in from another app
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit import\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bring data in from another app
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object per result, with `"v":1`, instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI colors
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
orbit\-import\-todoist(1)
Import active Todoist items. The token is read from ORBIT_TODOIST_TOKEN or stdin, used once and never stored. Without \-\-yes it only previews the mapping
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  orbit import todoist
  orbit import todoist \-\-map 2201=project:Home/Garden \-\-yes
